---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '2026-09-20';
const contact = 'privacy@kozh.dev';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hermes — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy of Hermes, a private personal assistant application."
>
  <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <div class="publication-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <main class="policy-shell" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
    <article class="policy">
      <p class="policy-kicker">Hermes</p>
      <h1 id="policy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>What Hermes is</h2>
      <p>
        Hermes is a private personal assistant operated by the owner of this site for himself and
        his family. It is not a public service: it has no sign-up, it is not offered to third
        parties, and only accounts explicitly approved by the owner can use it.
      </p>

      <h2>Google data the application accesses</h2>
      <p>
        With the account owner's consent, Hermes accesses the following data in that person's own
        Google account:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google Calendar — to read, create, update and delete events and reminders.</li>
        <li>
          Google Drive — to store and read files the owner asks it to keep, such as receipt photos.
        </li>
        <li>
          Google Sheets and Google Docs — to read and write the owner's own spreadsheets and
          documents, such as expense logs and task journals.
        </li>
        <li>Gmail — to read, send and organise mail when the owner asks it to.</li>
        <li>Google Contacts — read-only, to resolve names to addresses.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the data is used</h2>
      <p>
        Data is used only to carry out requests made by the account owner, for example adding a
        calendar event or appending a row to a spreadsheet. It is not used for advertising,
        profiling, analytics or any purpose unrelated to the request.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the data is processed and stored</h2>
      <p>
        Hermes runs on a server controlled by the owner. OAuth tokens are stored on that server with
        access restricted to the application. To understand and answer a request, the text of the
        request and the data needed to fulfil it may be sent to language model providers acting as
        processors. No Google user data is sold, and none is shared with anyone else.
      </p>

      <h2>Limited Use</h2>
      <p>
        Hermes' use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
          >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
        >, including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Data stays in the owner's Google account; Hermes keeps working copies only as long as a
        request requires, plus conversation history on the owner's server. Access can be revoked at
        any time at
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>,
        which immediately invalidates the application's tokens. Stored data is deleted on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions and deletion requests: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-shell {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    padding-top: 116px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }

  .policy {
    width: min(100%, 760px);
    padding: clamp(22px, 5vw, 56px) clamp(6px, 3vw, 18px);
    color: var(--paper-ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .policy-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--paper-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-ui-label);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--paper-ink);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .policy-meta {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-ui-label);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 36px 0 8px;
    color: var(--paper-ink);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--paper-accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .policy-shell {
      padding-top: 92px;
      padding-bottom: 42px;
    }
  }
</style>
